cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "qphys: quantum formalism as a modeling language"
abstract: >-
  Two sub-projects under one set of honesty rules. `collapse` asks whether a
  model built from the quantum formalism (Kraus operators, hidden quantum
  Markov models, quantum causal states) predicts or represents a real time
  series more efficiently than the best classical model at matched capacity.
  `lawlearn` asks whether the speed of light can be read out of a network
  trained on slow motion alone, and what actually extrapolates.
